# Cline Project Rules - Fresh Gen2 Amplify Todo App

This file provides context for the Cline extension to work effectively with this project.

## Project Overview
- **Name**: Fresh Gen2 Amplify Todo App
- **Root Directory**: `/home/tbaltzakis/gen2-comparison-fresh`
- **Environment**: WSL2 (Linux/Ubuntu)
- **Framework**: Next.js 15 (App Router)
- **Backend**: AWS Amplify Gen2 (TypeScript-first)
- **Styling**: Tailwind CSS + shadcn/ui
- **Package Manager**: pnpm

## Directory Structure
- `src/app/`: Next.js pages and API routes.
- `amplify/`: Amplify Gen2 backend configuration (auth, data).
- `src/components/`: Reusable React components.
- `doc/`: Project documentation (including `WSL_GUIDE.md`).
- `tests/`: Playwright E2E tests.

## Development Workflow
- **Start Dev Server**: `pnpm dev` (Runs on port 3001)
- **Amplify Sandbox**: `npx ampx sandbox`
- **WSL Check**: `pnpm wsl:check`
- **Run Tests**: `npx playwright test`

## WSL Specifics
- Always use absolute paths within the Linux file system: `/home/tbaltzakis/gen2-comparison-fresh`.
- Do not use `/mnt/c/` paths for development as it degrades performance.
- The app is accessed via `localhost:3001` on the Windows host.

## Coding Standards
- Use TypeScript for all new files.
- Follow the existing component structure in `src/components/`.
- Use shadcn/ui components for UI elements.
- Ensure all backend changes are made in the `amplify/` directory.
